  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Address urgent humanitarian needs of refugees and refugee returnees entering Ethiopia due to the conflict in Sudan (UNHCR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This multi-sectoral project aims to provide critical life-saving protection services and assistance to refugees, returnees, and affected members of the host community in Kurmuk and Metema. The project will alleviate protection risks and threats through protection activities, including timely registration and documentation of refugees, emergency communal shelter set-up in the transit centers, WASH activities, including emergency water provision through water trucking and the development of a durable water supply system and provision of food security and of basic and emergency health and nutrition services. UNHCR&apos;s emergency assistance will benefit 64,610 individuals, including 27,000 men, 27,500 women, 5,055 boys and 5,055 girls, and including 3,523 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
